Subject: [PATCH 51/51] PC5: a directory listed by its NT name when Wine's server
 keeps no Unix name for it (Wine patch 0936)

Wine enters a directory to list it by the Unix name the in-process
server keeps for its handle (patch 0140). When the server keeps none,
the listing failed with "invalid handle": Heroes of Might and Magic:
Olden Era couldn't list StreamingAssets\maps\Story_maps, so its modes
did nothing and Load Game emptied the screen. The directory is now
entered by the Unix name of the NT name the server keeps for every
file, and one still not entered is logged with the reason.
